    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The preceding derivations help clarify the meaning of Falconer’s maternal effect coefficient $ m $, and also suggest ways to estimate it. First, $ m $ is seen to be the difference between the two parent-offspring regressions",
      "source_page": 719,
      "printed_page": 699,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter23:p021:b17"
      ],
      "bbox": [
